Description: Host docked DevTools in the tab's content area on Android
 The docked DevTools WebContents covers the content area of the tab and the
 tab's contents are drawn on top of it, resized and moved to the bounds the
 frontend requested, like the desktop's DevToolsWebView/ContentsLayoutManager:
 .
  * StaticTabSceneLayer draws the DevTools layer behind the clipped and
    offset tab contents.
  * DockedDevToolsHost places the DevTools ContentView over the content area
    for input/IME, letting input over the inspected contents pass through to
    the tab, and pins the browser controls while docked.
  * CompositorViewHolder sizes the tab's WebContents to the inspected bounds
    and offsets touch events accordingly.
